00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:46.360
Share buybacks occur when a company uses cash

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:47.920
to repurchase its own shares,

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:50.340
which mechanically reduces the float,

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:53.920
and often lifts earnings per share while supporting prices

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:56.180
when other fundamentals are stable.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:02:01.920
With $665 billion already authorized this year,

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:05.320
the tactic is especially relevant in a mixed market

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:07.500
where organic growth is uncertain

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:09.860
and companies with strong free cash flow

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:13.020
can return capital directly to shareholders.

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:17.440
Investors can implement this by screening for firms

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:19.560
that have active repurchase programs

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:21.980
and sufficient cash generation.

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:25.120
Most Canadian platforms including Questrade

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:28.260
and Interactive Brokers let users filter

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:30.440
by share repurchase authorization

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:34.740
and cross check the latest 10Q or management discussion

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:37.100
and analysis for remaining capacity.

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:40.580
Historically, the strategy has delivered excess returns

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:43.540
in sideways or modestly rising markets

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:47.500
when buybacks are funded from operations rather than debt.

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:51.320
However, it can backfire if management over pays

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:54.920
or if the company later faces a liquidity crunch.

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:59.160
The key risk metric is the ratio of buyback spend

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:00.940
to operating cash flow.

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:04.680
Anything above 50% for consecutive quarters

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:06.300
warrants extra scrutiny.

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:11.400
Canadian investors can apply the same screen inside a TFSA

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.780
to capture the tax-free compounding effect

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:15.360
of a reduced share count.

