00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:37.220
in a month, lifting the total footprint

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:41.500
to eight locations in the state and 74 nationally.

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:44.740
The technical setup shows the stock reacting

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:47.120
to operational expansion news,

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:51.660
so monitor for volume confirmation above the 20-day average

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:55.260
and nearest resistance from recent consolidation range.

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:59.960
We assess the risk as medium given that the cannabis sector

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:02.360
remains sensitive to regulatory shifts

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:04.140
and state level competition.

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:08.080
Set a stop loss 6 to 8% below entry

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:10.220
to cap single position drawdown.

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:15.600
The target is plus 3% to plus 6% over the weekly horizon,

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:18.180
assuming continued rollout momentum.

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:21.120
This is a medium confidence setup

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:25.360
because operational expansion provides a tangible growth catalyst

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:27.580
but broader sector volatility

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:30.340
and limited price history on the new locations

00:04:30.340 --> 00:04:31.800
introduce uncertainty.

00:04:32.420 --> 00:04:36.620
What this teaches is how to evaluate retail expansion catalysts

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:38.680
in emerging consumer sectors

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:41.300
by focusing on unit growth metrics

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:43.560
rather than headline revenue alone.

