00:06:20.180 --> 00:06:22.620
Imagine you notice DuPont shares jump

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:25.400
after the company reported its latest quarter

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:28.060
and you placed a market order at the open.

00:06:28.840 --> 00:06:31.920
The fill price reflected not just the headline number,

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:34.540
but also how the market interpreted revenue

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:36.360
versus earnings quality,

00:06:36.920 --> 00:06:39.640
forward guidance and balance sheet health.

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:43.520
Revenue growth tells you whether the top line is expanding

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:47.520
while earnings and EPS reveal how much of that growth

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:51.180
actually reaches shareholders after costs and taxes.

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:54.980
A bid on EPS alone can be misleading

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:57.460
if it stems from one-time tax items

00:06:57.460 --> 00:07:01.280
or aggressive cost-cutting rather than sustainable sales.

00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:05.680
The forward PE ratio and management's own guidance

00:07:05.680 --> 00:07:09.080
on the next quarter or year are usually more important

00:07:09.080 --> 00:07:11.240
than the backward looking beat or miss.

00:07:12.180 --> 00:07:15.660
On the balance sheet, rising debt paired with declining cash

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:19.020
is a red flag even when earnings look fine.

00:07:19.780 --> 00:07:23.400
Free cash flow that exceeds reported net income signals

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:27.000
real cash generation rather than accounting optics.

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:30.280
Professionals always read the management discussion

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:33.500
and analysis section for the company's own assessment

00:07:33.500 --> 00:07:36.740
of risks and outlook instead of relying solely

00:07:36.740 --> 00:07:38.780
on the press release bullet points.

00:07:39.820 --> 00:07:42.100
The biggest mistake retail investors make

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:45.940
is treating any earnings beat as an automatic buy signal.

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:50.340
Instead, always compare actual results and guidance

00:07:50.340 --> 00:07:52.360
against consensus estimates

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:56.360
and check whether the beat was driven by sustainable operations

00:07:56.360 --> 00:07:58.180
or transitory factors.

